   "flags": [],
   "note": "Most stable site: fcc hollow, preferred over hcp by 0.05 eV. Literature GGA values for fcc O/Cu(111) relative to the O atom: -4.3 eV (PW91, Xu & Mavrikakis, Surf. Sci. 494 (2001) 131, abstract) and -5.000 eV (fcc) / -4.905 eV (hcp) (PBE, arXiv:2505.12914). Our -4.84 eV and the fcc-over-hcp ordering fall within that spread. Premise: no direct experimental value exists for an isolated O atom reference, so this is a PBE-level (0 K, no ZPE) quantity. MLIP caveat: the O atom energy is the model's fitted per-element E0, not a spin-polarized triplet PBE atom calculation. That reference was validated indirectly: the Cu cohesive energy using the same type of atom reference is 3.501 eV vs 3.49 exp, and the O2 binding energy (6.29 eV) is PBE-like. Uncertainty +-0.3 eV covers MLIP-vs-PBE error including the atom-reference E0, the spread in published GGA values, and the size and coverage effects (<0.07 eV). It does NOT cover GGA functional error: PBE overbinds O2 by about 1 eV, so the gas-atom reference energy is itself functional-dependent. Combining our E_ads vs 1/2 O2 (-1.69 eV) with the experimental O2 De (5.21 eV) gives about -4.30 eV, an experiment-anchored estimate.",
